    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52), who represent our strongest offensive upside against Nick Martinez and Bailey Ober, respectively. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 13% boost derived from dynamic platoon splits, while **Dylan Beavers**\u2014a high-priority target due to our focus on speed\u2014capitalizes on an excellent matchup against an Ober delivery profile that remains susceptible to base stealers. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) also ranks among our elite starters today; his matchup against Mason Barnett in a favorable park, coupled with a batting order promotion to the #2 spot, drives his efficiency score to the top of our 1B/MI depth chart.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Braden Montgomery**, whose score of 53.85 was bolstered by a strong SP skill matchup against Nick Lodolo. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the positional flexibility and higher floor offered by **Luis Arraez** (57.83) and **Zack Gelof** (58.32). While **Braden Montgomery** shows promise, his proximity to the bench threshold, combined with the volatility of facing a left-handed arm like Lodolo, led to his exclusion in favor of starters with more guaranteed lineup positions. We also continue to monitor **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (57.41), whose base projection remains elite despite a significant -17% adjustment for facing a tough Drew Anderson; we keep him in the lineup due to his high ceiling, though his score is notably suppressed today.\n\nInvestors should note that we are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, introducing variance into our projections. **Yainer Diaz** (51.88) and **Cal Raleigh** (52.83) currently sit on the low end of our efficiency scale, largely due to unfavorable order positioning and SP matchup constraints. We will monitor official lineups closely, particularly for **Justin Crawford** (56.15); while he provides necessary stolen base upside, his proximity to the 50-point threshold warrants caution should his batting order drop below the #7 spot. We are avoiding the sub-40 range entirely today to protect our game caps, benching **JJ Bleday** (39.21) after he failed to clear the efficiency bar against Sean Burke.",
